content.text:
I've rewritten `ec-ai-corpus`'s history to drop the old full-text earnings tables, added the note you asked for, and added the permacomputing rule to `AGENTS.md`. Nothing is pushed.

**What the rewrite did:**
- Every old full-text version of the three earnings-call tables is gone from the branch. That's 33.5 MB, and the packed repo goes from 113 MiB to 82 MiB.
- The files at the tip of the branch are identical to before. Everything already on GitHub and the paper's v0 commit (`1afb042`) keep their hashes.
- 68 unpushed commits got new hashes.
- My first attempt also changed hashes already on GitHub, because filter-repo strips the GitHub signature on the repo's first commit. I redid it limited to the commits after the first full-text table, which fixed that.
- Other sessions' uncommitted and staged work wasn't touched.

**The note** is `docs/history-rewrite-2026-11-04.md` (cdeb6b2, 29403f7). It records:
- what was removed and why, citing Praxis P1;
- how the rewrite was done;
- the size before and after;
- a lookup table from all 68 old commit hashes to their new ones.

It also lists what's still bigger than it needs to be:
- the Wikipedia article text, which is stored twice;
- a 5.5 MB TSV of ids and flags;
- 40 MB of model-output parquets;
- 18 MB of Epoch CSVs.

I updated the two old anthropic-pbc hashes that Praxis's open questions cite.

**Permacomputing in `AGENTS.md`:** there's a new first convention, "**Small.** Permacomputing: keep everything as small as possible…", which points to Praxis `PRINCIPLES.md` P1 (7674ed3). The other session's uncommitted lines in that file are untouched.

**Before the full-text tables came out:** the earnings tables now commit only ids, offsets and hashes. Tracked `corpus/earnings-calls/` went from 35.4 MB to 6.5 MB, and every downstream output rebuilt byte-identical.

**Checks after all of it:**
- the DAG is 36/36 ok;
- the catalog is current;
- the attestations verify;
- `ec_extract verify` reports 0 bad;
- the 54 control tests pass;
- the edition `--check` passes.

**The rebuilt deck PDF is open now.** Its numbers are the corrected ones (79 companies, the per-passage rate, 32.2% vs 5.7%). `DECK.md`, `deck/*.svg` and `deck/STAMP.json` are uncommitted in the working tree for you to review and commit.

**Old copies still on this machine:**
- I removed my own finished worktrees and branches.
- Ten other agent worktrees still hold the old history. Three of them are locked, and some may belong to other sessions, so I left them.
- Entire's local session checkpoints also still point at old commits. They stay local, because pushing them is off.

None of these leave the machine unless someone pushes those branches.

